{%- comment -%}
  The currency switch. The prices on the page are in the page's own currency;
  each also carries its amount in every other currency the page offers, and
  `assets/currency.js` puts one of those in its place when a buyer asks.

  It is in the page hidden: without the script there is nothing to press,
  and the page is what it was rendered as. It is not in the page at all when
  there is nothing to switch between — no prices, or one currency.

  The buttons say the currencies' own codes, which are the same in every
  language; the group's name is from the language pack. The layout that
  renders this also loads the script.
{%- endcomment -%}
{% if plugins.shop.currencies.size > 1 %}
<div class="currency" role="group" aria-label="{{ t.currency }}" data-currency="{{ plugins.shop.currency | downcase }}" hidden>
  {% for code in plugins.shop.currencies %}<button type="button" value="{{ code | downcase }}" aria-pressed="{% if code == plugins.shop.currency %}true{% else %}false{% endif %}">{{ code }}</button>{% endfor %}
</div>
{% endif %}
